ENTRY            D6443   20260817   20261124   20261124       D153
SUBENT        D6443001   20260817   20261124   20261124       D153
BIB                 10         30
TITLE      Systematic investigation of channel-coupling effects
            on elastic, inelastic, and neutron-transfer channels
            in 6Li+159Tb
AUTHOR     (S.Bhattacharjee, P.Biswas, A.Gupta, M.K.Pradhan,
            N.Deshmukh, P.Basu, V.V.Parkar, S.Santra,
            K.Ramachandran, A.Chatterjee, S.Roy, A.Mukherjee)
INSTITUTE  (3INDSAH,3INDTRM)
           (3INDIND) Homi Bhabha National Institute, Mumbai
REFERENCE  (J,PR/C,106,064612,2022)
           #doi:10.1103/PhysRevC.106.064612
FACILITY   (VDGT,3INDTAT) 14UD BARC-TIFR Pelletron-Linac
SAMPLE     A self-supporting target of 159Tb foil having a
            thickness ~700 ug/cm2
DETECTOR   (TELES,SIBAR,SIBAR) Four silicon surface barrier
            detector telescope with different thicknesses: T1
            with delta E=25 um and E=500 um T2 with delta E=25 um
            and E=2000 um T3 with delta E=25 um and E=3000 um T4
            with delta E=25 um and E=2000 um were employed in an
            angular range 20-160 degree.
           The Si surface barrier detectors used in the experiment
            have an estimated energy resolution of ~150 keV.
           (SIBAR) Two monitor detectors at fixed angles of
            +/-10 degree with respect to beam direction for
            normalization purpose.
METHOD     (EDE)
ERR-ANALYS (DATA-ERR) Errors in the fit parameters and statistical
            data errors were included in the overall error
            calculation for both elastic and inelastic components.
HISTORY    (20260619R) Data received from S.Bhattacharjee
           (20260817C) A.Gandhi
ENDBIB              30
